OL,3,GNEWSAThe charity building young
OL,4,Apeople's confidence
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Olivia first came to an
OL,7,Fafter-school club run by Liberty
OL,8,FJamboree, she would hide behind her
OL,9,Fmum's legs and wouldn't really talk or
OL,10,Fcome in.
OL,12,FFive years on, the 13-year-old, who has
OL,13,FDown's syndrome, said the charity,
OL,14,Fbased in Lichfield, Staffordshire, was
OL,15,Flike "family" and she felt "happy" and
OL,16,F"alive."
OL,18,FIt's a change her mum, Sarah, said had
OL,19,Fbeen transformational, helping her
OL,20,Fdaughter to grow in confidence and
OL,21,Findependence.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
